// Title: Cloud Instance Metadata API Query for Credential Theft
// Sigma ID: a1b3839d-705c-48b2-9d95-b773944bcdd9
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Gideon Opukeme
// Date: 2026-10-18 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552, T1552.005
// Description: Detects queries to the cloud instance metadata service (169.254.169.254) using curl or wget.
//   Adversaries query this endpoint from compromised cloud instances to retrieve credentials and
//   other secrets such as IAM role credentials.
// False positives:
//   - Cloud-init and legitimate monitoring agents that query instance metadata for configuration
//   - On-premises tooling that happens to reference the link-local address
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1552.005/T1552.005.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/258ad25218376be68f6342d7ce6c29a99f5f020a/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_cloud_imds_credential_theft.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/curl" or FolderPath endswith "/wget") and ProcessCommandLine contains "169.254.169.254"
